<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Based on FOB Omaha basis carlot prices of fabricated beef cuts and on industry yields as of 1500, boxed beef steady to weak on light to moderate demand and offerings. Select and Choice rib, chuck and round cuts steady to weak, while the loin cuts generally steady.</p>
<p>Beef trimmings not established. -- USDA</p>
<p>138 Fab Lds   CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>    50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>39 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     108.61	108.91	101.91	101.06</p>
<p>Change	   -0.04	  0.04	  0.09	 -0.38</p>
<p>Rib	  169.61	170.98	156.74	156.15</p>
<p>Chuck	 75.89	 74.48	 76.57	 72.58</p>
<p>Round	 95.28	 95.28	 92.51	 92.51</p>
<p>Loin	 169.73	172.40	147.03	148.89</p>
<p>Brisket     64.56	 64.56	 63.36	 63.36</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  67.17	 67.09	 67.42	 67.24</p>
<p>Flank	 59.07	 59.07	 58.86	 58.86</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
